      "stones": "B:pd W:nc",
      "toPlay": "B",
      "name": "4-4 point · low approach",
      "notes": [
        "{{TR:O17|{{White}}'s low approach}} to {{TR:Q16|the 4-4 stone}}, along the top. The approach from the other side is the same position mirrored. Small knight approach (keima kakari). It threatens to slide into the corner at {{CR:Q18}} or to extend along the top, and it is the approach that strong players and AI programs prefer."
      ],
      "values": {
        "evaluation": 0,
        "status": "start",
        "tags": [
          "approach",
          "basic joseki"
        ],
        "difficulty": "20k",
        "summary": "{{White}} approaches the 4-4 stone with a small knight's move, the most common star point approach. {{Black}} answers by extending (small knight or one-space high), pincering, kicking, attaching, or playing elsewhere. Sources: 44PointLowApproach, 44PointLowApproachLowExtensionSlide33, 44PointLowApproachHighExtension, 44PointLowApproachAttach, 44PointOneSpaceLowPincerInvasionBlock.",
